87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The Loan EMI Priority Manager is a Java-based application developed to manage loan applications and prioritize them for processing. It is a Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project that uses a Priority Queue, Binary Search Tree \(BST\), HashMap, ArrayList and file handling.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The Priority Queue is used to process loan applications according to their assigned priority. Applications with higher priority scores are processed first. When two applications have the same priority, the application submitted earlier is processed first. A Binary Search Tree organizes loan applications according to their loan amount, while a HashMap provides fast searching through unique application IDs.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The system calculates the monthly Equated Monthly Installment \(EMI\) using the loan amount, annual interest rate and repayment tenure. It also checks loan affordability by comparing the EMI with the applicant's monthly income. Application details and status changes are stored in a text file named loan_applications.txt.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
